# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets and
# engagement data out of the image entirely.
**/.git
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]

# Never. These are the database, the session key and the DSN.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite*
**/.secret
**/pg.env
**/.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key

docs/
.github/
**/*.md
!README.md

# Tests do not run in the image and nothing imports them. Not for
# size — measured, and it is 105.1 MB either way, because they are
# small text files. The reason is that a deployed image should contain
# what it runs: 18 files of test fixtures full of credential-shaped
# strings like "root-password-1" are a thing for an incident responder
# to rule out at the worst possible moment, and they are not needed
# here to rule in.
backend/tests/
backend/runtests.py
**/*_test.go
